  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/omnesoft/tika-content-detector-dotnet",
  "published": "2026-10-14T16:48:08.09Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Detection is now a port of Apache Tika 3.3.1's engine: nested magic rules, root-XML rules, Tika's file-name rule, and container checks for ZIP and OLE2 formats. Adds types for Autodesk Inventor and Fusion files and a rule for SolidWorks 2015 files, and makes IGES and VRML text formats so that their file names decide the type. Breaking changes: MimeType.MagicPatterns, MimeType.MagicPattern, MagicMatcher, GlobMatcher, ZipContainerInspector and TarContainerInspector are removed, along with GlobPattern.Matches, CaseInsensitive and Weight. MimeTypesRepository.GetMimeTypesWithMagicPatterns is now GetMimeTypesWithMagicRules. A type name with parameters is written as \"type/subtype; key=value\", and some files now detect as such a subtype, for example \"image/vnd.dxf; format=ascii\". IsSubtypeOf follows aliases and Tika's implied parents, so text/csv is now a subtype of application/octet-stream. Loading two unrelated types that share a file-name pattern, or a type whose parent is not a media type, throws MimeTypeException and stores nothing of that type. The detection_method metadata is one of container, magic, magic+filename, text, text+filename, filename or default, Confidence follows from it, and the priority metadata key is gone. Container formats need a stream that can seek. The CLI's JSON fields hasMagicPatterns and magicPatternCount are now hasMagicRules and magicRuleCount.",
